course: dictionary
lesson: 15703
title: Toothpick: one word, two jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A toothpick is a small, thin stick with a sharp point. Its name tells you its first job: a tooth pick is something that picks things out from your teeth. «After lunch, Sam used a toothpick to get a bit of bread out from between his teeth.»
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Toothpick has a second meaning too: a tool for holding small pieces of food together, or for testing whether a cake is cooked. «Mum pushed a toothpick into the cake, and it came out clean, so the cake was ready.» The words around the word tell you which meaning is being used.
explain: Context clues help you choose. «The party sandwiches were held together with toothpicks.» The words sandwiches and party tell you the toothpicks are for food, not for teeth. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A toothpick is a small thin stick of wood or plastic with a point.
fact: Toothpicks are used to remove bits of food from between your teeth.
fact: Toothpicks can hold small pieces of food together, such as sandwiches and party snacks.
fact: A cook pokes a toothpick into a cake; if it comes out clean, the cake is cooked.
fact: Toothpicks are sharp, so never put them in your ears, and keep them away from small children.
exercise: «After lunch, Sam used a toothpick to get a bit of bread out from between his teeth.» What is the toothpick used for here? | To write a letter | To hold a shoe together | *To remove food from between your teeth | To paint a wall
exercise: Mum pushed a toothpick into the cake, and it came out clean. What does this tell her? | The cake needs more sugar | The oven is too cold | The toothpick is broken | *The cake is cooked
exercise: Why should a toothpick never go in your ear? | Because it will make your ears glow | *Because it is sharp and could hurt you | Because it will make your ears grow | Because it tastes of mint
test: «The party sandwiches were held together with toothpicks.» What were the toothpicks doing? | *Holding the food together | Cleaning the table | Mending a broken plate | Scraping off the crumbs
test: In school, the class used toothpicks and marshmallows to build a pyramid. What are the toothpicks used for in this lesson? | *To build shapes | To eat the marshmallows | To stir hot chocolate | To write their names
exam: Which sentence uses toothpick to mean a tool for testing a cake? | *Dad poked a toothpick into the cake, and it came out clean | Sam stuck a toothpick in his shoe | The toothpick lay under the table | The toothpick was cold and wet
